.Nm dtfl_ddir_server_peek ,
.Nm dtfl_ddir_server_list
.Nd host interpreted DDIR programs that share results by name
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/server.h
.Ft dtfl_ddir_server *
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_new "FILE *out"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_free "dtfl_ddir_server *s"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_epoch "const dtfl_ddir_server *s"
.Ft bool
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_has_trace "const dtfl_ddir_server *s" "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_install "dtfl_ddir_server *s" "const char *name" "const dtfl_ddir_program *program"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_feed "dtfl_ddir_server *s" "const char *prog" "size_t input" "const dtfl_ddir_value *key" "const dtfl_ddir_value *val" "bool has_time" "uint64_t time" "int64_t diff"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_tick "dtfl_ddir_server *s"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_drop "dtfl_ddir_server *s" "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_peek "dtfl_ddir_server *s" "const char *trace" "const dtfl_ddir_value *key"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_list "const dtfl_ddir_server *s"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A DDIR server hosts interpreted DDIR programs in one running computation
and lets them share results by name.
Programs are installed one at a time; each may import traces that other
programs have exported, so a consumer maintains a computation
incrementally over a producer's output.
This is the interpreter-driven form of the old
.Ql dd_server :
.Dq install
renders a DDIR program against a live registry, not a loaded shared
object.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_new
creates a server with the host clock at epoch zero.
The
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_peek
and
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_list
output and the command status lines are written to
.Fa out ,
or to standard output when
.Fa out
is
.Dv NULL .
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_free
releases the server and every program it holds.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_install
builds the dataflow of
.Fa program
under
.Fa name ,
wiring each root trace import to a registered trace and registering each
export's trace for later imports.
A trace import that names a recipe
.Pq Ql random:nodes=N,edges=E , Ql iota:N , or Ql clock
installs its generated source on demand; generated sources are
content-addressed, so two importers of the same recipe share one source.
The server keeps a private copy of
.Fa program .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_feed
stages an update to positional input
.Fa input
of program
.Fa prog :
it adds
.Fa key
with value
.Fa val
.Pq or unit when Fa val No is Dv NULL
at multiplicity
.Fa diff ,
at time
.Fa time
when
.Fa has_time
is set, otherwise at the current epoch.
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_tick
closes the current epoch, advances every input, and runs to quiescence.
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_drop
evicts a program, refusing (and changing nothing) if any trace it
publishes still has a live importer.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_peek
prints the consolidated contents of a registered trace as of the current
epoch, optionally restricted to one
.Fa key .
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_list
prints the registry: the epoch, the published traces with their importer
counts, and the installed programs.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_new
returns a server, or
.Dv NULL
only through the panic hook on allocation failure.
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_install ,
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_feed ,
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_drop
and
.Fn dtfl_ddir_server_peek
return zero on success or a
.Dv DTFL_E Ns *
code, with a message through
.Xr dtfl_last_error_detail 3 .
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
The upstream server is multi-worker, circulating commands to every worker
through a timely
.Vt Sequencer .
This server runs a single in-process worker and dispatches every command
on the calling thread, which replays the example sessions.
It does not compact published traces
.Pq the public trace handle has no compaction setter ,
so a long run holds full history; results are unaffected.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl-ddir 1 ,
.Xr dtfl_ddir_parse 3
